how can nintendo make animal crossing  new horizons even better  in today's video i'll offer up some  suggestions on how nintendo can take an  already fantastic game and make it even  better  people of the internet retro racking  tour here and welcome back to another  animal crossing new horizons video  if we're meeting for the first time i'm  just a dad who loves games and the  stories they tell  we post videos twice a week here on  youtube and today is all about making  animal crossing  even better than it already is here are  five quality of life changes i'd love to  see nintendo try and implement within  the next few months  of course i want to hear from you guys  as well so let me know what other ideas  you have  in the comments below number one buying  in bulk  okay we might as well start with an  obvious one here right why don't we have  the ability to buy in bulk on  any item sure buying in bulk is in the  game currently but only for specific  items and only in amounts preset by  nintendo  flowers and tree saplings for example  can be purchased as a pack of one  or five but why not let us buy 20 or  7 all at once turnips of course are  completely separate items sold by a  different vendor those are sold in  bundles of 10.  but again why not open this up and allow  players to purchase items in any amount  provided they have room of course  if i want to stock up on fishing poles  then let me buy 10 all at once rather  than having me place 10 separate orders  with tommy and timmy of course you could  also apply this to the shopping app  which you unlock on your phone later in  the game or even the kiosk that is in  resident services throughout the game  number two more visibility for item sets  at the heart of animal crossing  is a game all about collecting  personally i'm way more inclined to  chase after an item when i see that i'm  missing part of a set  so why not give us a little sneak peek  at some of the items we're missing out  on  let's say you craft or find a furniture  item that's part of a larger set  what if at that point you could then  look through your recipe book to see the  recipes in the set that you still lack  or if the item is only available to buy  show us the other items that we can  purchase from that particular set  they could even take this a step further  and let us know all the possible ways  that we can go about obtaining the item  at least for me this would be a pretty  powerful way to encourage me to hunt and  search for even more  items and thus increase replayability  and yes i know you can view these items  online but the vast majority of animal  crossing players most likely stick to  the in-game tools available  number three daily story lines so one of  the biggest critiques of animal crossing  is how quickly you can burn out doing  the same tasks over and over again  and while i don't expect animal crossing  to ever offer some insane branching  narrative  nor do i believe it should i do think  there are ways nintendo could weave a  bit more story into the game to help  keep things fresh and interesting  my idea is something i'm calling daily  story lines  the concept here is that each day would  have a randomized storyline involving  one or several of your villagers  now this could be fairly simple and  straightforward but still staying within  the current confines of the game let's  say octavian decides to host a party one  evening and needs your help getting  ready for it  as part of this storyline you'd be  tasked with inviting other villagers  designing a special decoration  helping set up for the party by  arranging furniture and maybe even  catching a few fish for the dinner  those are just a few of the basic ideas  i have but i think you get the idea  of course nintendo could sweeten the pot  even further by offering a reward at the  end  maybe you could even choose between  three different rewards upon completing  the final section of the storyline am i  asking for too much  i don't think i'm asking for too much  moving on to number four  crafting multiples of the same item how  many times have you  sighed while spamming away on the a  button waiting for your items to finish  crafting i'm looking at you manila clams  this is one of those small changes that  would really make a huge difference in  our day-to-day enjoyment of the game  if you have enough materials the game  should allow you to craft as many as you  want  all at once i'd even be fine with the  actual crafting process taking a few  seconds longer if you're crafting  multiples of an item  but the process of having to go into the  menu and select your item each time  grows tedious and boring rather quickly  and just to be clear here i'm only  talking about when you want to craft  multiple copies of the same  item so you'd still need to go into the  craft menu each time you wanted to craft  a different item  number five terraforming improvements  terraforming is the best addition to an  animal crossing game  in years maybe ever yeah i said it  having the ability to reshape your  island make your own cliffs and alter  your waterways  offers an incredible amount of  replayability and flexibility for making  your island exactly as you want  and of course we want even more sorry  nintendo it's all out of love  as wonderful as terraforming is it's  incredibly  time consuming there's no way to make  large scale changes  you'll need to make any modifications  tile by tile  by tile that's right one tile at a time  you're also pretty severely limited with  your bridges and inclines  you can have eight of each but it's not  the number of them that's so much of a  problem it's the fact that it takes an  entire day to add or remove one of them  but let's ignore the problems with  bridges and inclines  and just focus on terraforming for a  moment if nintendo could figure out a  way to let you make  large scale changes rather than going  tile by tile  it would be a huge win maybe they even  start small by letting us alter 1  4 or 16 tiles at a time so at least with  that setting you could create a large  cliff or waterway  much faster than going one tile at a  time  another idea that would save creators  time is to offer a dedicated button for  the two types of edges on your cliffs  and rivers  as it is now you have to press the  button twice at just the right angle to  shape the edges how you want them  better yet give us even more edging  options if you'd like to see any of  these ideas implemented into new  horizons give me a thumbs up on the  video here and don't forget to comment  down below  letting me know what other ideas you  have thank you so much for watching i'll  talk to you again soon
 

